{
  "id": "site.holy_spirit",
  "name": "Holy Spirit church and almshouse",
  "name_1343": "Heiliggeist: parish church and almshouse (Pühavaimu)",
  "confidence": "attested institution (priest 1316/1319, almshouse 1334); 1343 fabric after the dossier: two-aisle hall, timber ceiling, vaults 1360",
  "sources": [
    "history/dossiers/religion/churches-and-religious-houses.md",
    "history/dossiers/topography/raekoja-plats-extents-1343.md"
  ],
  "period_notes": [
    "Two-aisle hall church with a flat timber ceiling: the star vaults and the tower are 1360, the baroque spire and the outside clock 17th century.",
    "Square choir on the north nave's axis; the almshouse (documented 1334) opens into the church so the sick follow the mass (layout plausible composite; bed count unknown).",
    "Stained glass: no Reval glass of 1343 survives; leaded pot-metal medallions and grisaille after 13th-14th-century Gotland parish churches, the cited model for Reval churches (plausible composite).",
    "Interior: lime wash with red-ochre false ashlar, frieze and consecration crosses; rood beam with crucifix; stone mensa high altar with a painted retable; font in the north nave; ledger slabs in the floor; congregation standing (no pews before the Reformation), wall benches for the weak."
  ],
  "presentation": [
    {
      "date": "2026-10-07",
      "by": "maintainer",
      "what": "west tower (1360) with a shingled helm",
      "reason": "recognisable silhouette for the market-edge parish; the baroque spire and clock stay out"
    }
  ],
